      "doctor_question": "Hello, welcome in. What brings you to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S001",
      "patient_response": "Well, hi there doc. I guess what brings me in is... I just keep messing up these little things lately. Like, the other day I was signing up for this class down at the senior center, and I wrote down the completely wrong time on the sheet. Which is a shame because they just remodeled the whole lobby area there where they keep the bulletin board. Used to have this awful green shag carpet, probably been there since 1974, and now it's this nice laminate flooring. My buddy Frank swears it's real oak, but I worked at a hardware store right out of high school, so I know laminate when I see it. \n\nBut anyway, yeah, just making mistakes. Like working out in the garage—I was measuring a board the other day, measured it once, and I still cut it a hair short because I just skipped right over the small print on the plans. It was supposed to be for a birdhouse. My granddaughter loves birds... she's seven now, lives out in Ohio. The state bird there is the cardinal, you know. Beautiful red feathers. But... wait, what did you ask me? Oh, right, why I'm here. Just... yeah, missing the small details on things like that.",
